## Method

Fetched raw HTML and, where it existed, the actual stylesheets via `curl` (WebFetch converts to markdown and destroys CSS, so every number below comes from source, not inference). 39 URLs returned HTTP 200 and were inspected. Notes below are grouped by what the site teaches.

---

## A. The crafted end — verbatim CSS

### Andrej Karpathy — https://karpathy.ai/ (+ /style.css)
34,286 bytes of HTML, one stylesheet, zero frameworks. His own note on the page: *"0 frameworks were used to make this simple responsive website because I am becoming seriously allergic to 500-pound websites."*

```css
body { font-family: sans-serif; font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.4; color: #333; }
@media (min-width: 992px) { .container { width: 970px; } }
.row { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(12, 1fr); }
#dpic  { grid-column: span 6; text-align: right; }
#ddesc { grid-column: span 6; padding-top: 40px; padding-left: 20px; }
#dpic img { width: 240px; height: 240px; border-radius: 120px; }
h1 { font-size: 34px; font-weight: normal; }
h2 { font-size: 18px; font-style: italic; color: #999; max-width: 300px; }
hr { height: 1px; border: 0;
     background-image: linear-gradient(left, rgba(0,0,0,0), rgba(0,0,0,0.75), rgba(0,0,0,0)); }
/* the timeline */
.timespan  { grid-column: span 1; font-size: 14px; text-align: right; color: #bbb; }
.ico       { grid-column: span 1; border-left: 2px solid #cfcfcf; position: relative; }
.entry-dot { position: absolute; top: 0; left: -8px; width: 10px; height: 10px;
             border-radius: 7px; background-color: #cfcfcf; border: 2px solid white; }
.desc      { grid-column: span 10; font-size: 17px; padding-left: 20px; }
/* publications */
.pub { font-size: 14px; border-left: 4px solid #aaa; padding: 2px 0 2px 10px; margin-bottom: 10px; }
```
Only two breakpoints (`min-width: 992px`, `max-width: 991px`), and `.hassets { display: none }` on mobile — decorative content simply removed. Hero HTML is 20 lines; the email is revealed on click via `#demail { opacity: 0; transition: opacity 0.7s }`.

### Jeffrey Heer — https://homes.cs.washington.edu/~jheer/ (+ /jheer.css)
Fixed 960px, no photo of himself, Verdana at ~10.4px. Old, and still one of the most distinctive academic pages alive because of two decisions: black links that only reveal colour on hover, and `h6` repurposed as small-caps section rules.

```css
body { max-width: 960px; min-width: 960px; width: 960px; padding: 12px 20px;
       font-family: Verdana, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 0.65em; line-height: 1.3em; }
h6 { font-size: 1.5em; font-weight: normal; font-variant: small-caps;
     letter-spacing: 1px; color: #777; line-height: 0.60em; }
#name { font-variant: small-caps; font-size: 1.5em; letter-spacing: 0.065em; }
a, a:visited, a:hover { color: #000; text-decoration: none; }
a:hover, a.nav:hover  { color: #53f; }
tr.visited td, tr.visited a { color: #888; }   /* he greys out things you've seen */
#info { float: left; width: 210px; }  #main { margin-left: 230px; }
.entry { clear: both; height: 80px; margin-bottom: 10px; }
.entry img { float: left; margin: 3px 8px 6px 1px; border-radius: 4px; }
.entry a:hover img { box-shadow: 2px 2px 18px #53f; }
#vita .margin { float: left; width: 115px; text-align: right; }
#vita .body   { margin-left: 135px; }
.announce { width: 190px; border: dashed 1px #ccc; }   /* the one 'card', and it's dashed */
```
Footer is a single lab image + "Visit the UW Interactive Data Lab for more! >>".

### David Blei — http://www.cs.columbia.edu/~blei/ (+ /static/blei.css)
The homepage HTML is **2,819 bytes**, complete. Tokenised, recently rewritten, and a good model for "modern minimal without being trendy."

```css
:root { --bg:#fff; --text:#111; --muted:#666; --accent:#005fa3;
        --font-body: Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;
        --space-xs:.5rem; --space-sm:.75rem; --space-md:1.5rem; --space-lg:2rem; }
body { margin: var(--space-lg); line-height: 1.6; }
.navigation { border-bottom: 1px solid #ddd; }
.nav-inner  { max-width: 900px; margin: 0 auto; display: flex; justify-content: space-between; }
.nav-avatar { width: 75px; height: 75px; border-radius: 50%; object-fit: cover; }
main { max-width: 800px; margin: var(--space-lg) auto; }
.bib2xhtml { list-style: disc inside; }   /* pubs are a plain bulleted list */
@media (max-width: 320px) { ... }          /* his ONLY media query */
```
Note the commented-out experiments left in the file (`/* --font-body: Georgia, serif; */`) — a human iterating, not a generator.

### Tufte CSS — https://edwardtufte.github.io/tufte-css/ (+ tufte.css)
```css
html { font-size: 15px; }
body { width: 87.5%; padding-left: 12.5%; max-width: 1400px;
       font-family: et-book, Palatino, "Palatino Linotype", "Palatino LT STD",
                    "Book Antiqua", Georgia, serif;
       background-color: #fffff8; color: #111; counter-reset: sidenote-counter; }
p, dl, ol, ul { font-size: 1.4rem; line-height: 2rem; }   /* 21px / 30px */
h1 { font-weight: 400; font-size: 3.2rem; line-height: 1; }
h2 { font-style: italic; font-weight: 400; font-size: 2.2rem; }
h3 { font-style: italic; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1.7rem; }
section > p, section > footer, section > table { width: 55%; }
.sidenote, .marginnote {
  float: right; clear: right; margin-right: -60%; width: 50%;
  margin-top: .3rem; font-size: 1.1rem; line-height: 1.3; position: relative; }
.sidenote-number:after { content: counter(sidenote-counter); font-size: 1rem; top: -0.5rem; }
figure.fullwidth figcaption { max-width: 40%; }
@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) { body { background-color:#151515; color:#ddd; } }
@media (max-width: 760px) { body { width: 84%; } /* sidenotes become toggles */ }
```

### gwern.net — https://gwern.net/ (+ /static/css/style.css, 310KB)
Typefaces: `Source Serif 4`, `Source Sans 3`, `IBM Plex Mono`, plus drop-cap display faces `Cheshire Initials`, `Goudy Initialen`, `Deutsche Zierschrift`, `Kanzlei Initialen`, `Yinit`, `Great Primer Uncials`. Ornaments shipped as data-URI SVG custom properties: `--GW-image-asterism-triplewhitestar-svg`, `--GW-image-japanesecrest-tsukinihoshi-dotlessmoon-svg`, `--GW-image-three-wavy-lines-ornament-left-svg`, `--GW-image-swiss-spiral-roll-svg`. Sidenotes capped at `--GW-sidenotes-max-width: 550px`. Heading self-links: `.heading a::after { content: "\00B6"; font-size: 0.75em; }`. Link popups: `--GW-popups-annotation-popup-min-width: 480px`. Mobile breakpoint `@media all and (max-width: 649px)`. Over-engineered for our purposes but the ornament + sidenote + pilcrow ideas are directly liftable.

### Maggie Appleton — https://maggieappleton.com/ (Astro)
```css
--font-body:  "Canela Text", serif;
--font-serif: "Canela Deck", serif;
--font-sans:  "Lato", sans-serif;
--color-cream:#f6f5f1;  --color-light-cream:#fcfbf7;  --color-tinted-cream:#e6e3e1;
--color-black:#353534;  --color-gray-400:#6b6864; --color-gray-600:#73706d;
--color-sea-blue:#04a5bb; --color-dark-sea-blue:#00758f;
--color-crimson:#5f023e;  --color-bright-crimson:#960462;
--color-crimson-10: color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-bright-crimson) 10%, transparent);
```
Utopia fluid type scale (min→max px): `--f--2: 14.5→15`, `--f--1: 16→16.5`, `--f-0: 20→22` (body), `--f-1: 25→28.6`, `--f-2: 30→36`, `--f-3: 39.06→44`, `--f-4: 46.87→56`, `--f-5: 57.6→81.8`. Space scale is a multiplier chain off `--fc-s` (`2xs = ×0.5, m = ×1.5, l = ×2, 2xl = ×4, 3xl = ×6, 4xl = ×8`). Full dark-mode token pairs for every colour. Six-stop layered shadows (`--box-shadow-sm` has six `rgba(40,10,0,…)` stops at `-10px` spread) — realistic, not the CSS-default drop shadow. The link underline is animated with clip-path:

```css
.styled-link:before {
  content:""; position:absolute; width:100%; height:1px; top:95%; left:0;
  background: var(--color-sea-blue); transform-origin: 50% 100%;
  transition: clip-path .3s, transform .3s cubic-bezier(.2,1,.8,1);
  clip-path: polygon(0% 0%,0% 100%,0 100%,0 0,100% 0,100% 100%,0 100%,0 100%,100% 100%,100% 0%); }
.styled-link:hover:before { transform: translate3d(0,2px,0) scale3d(1,2,1); clip-path: polygon(…); }
```

### Matt Might — https://matt.might.net/ (+ /css/mm2.css)
```css
body { font-family: Palatino; font-size: 125%; color: #505050; background-color: white; }
div#main { margin-left:auto; margin-right:auto; max-width: 35em; }
div#main-content { line-height: 1.2; }
blockquote { border-left: 10px solid #ccc; margin: 1.5em 10px; padding: .5em 30px; }
blockquote:before { color:#ccc; font-size:4em; line-height:.1em; vertical-align:-.4em; }
```
`35em` at 20px = ~700px = ~66 characters. This is the whole design.

### Julia Evans — https://jvns.ca/ (+ /stylesheets/screen.css)
```css
.serif, body { font-family: "PT Serif", Georgia, Times, serif; line-height: 1.25em; color:#000; }
.heading, article h1..h6, nav, .pagination, .header-links { font-family: "Montserrat", sans-serif; }
nav, .pagination, .header-links { font-weight: bold; text-transform: uppercase; }
#wrap > header h1 { font-family:"PT Sans"; font-weight:700; font-size: 4em; }
#wrap > header h2 { font-family:"Alegreya","PT Serif",serif; }
#wrap { width: 70%; max-width: 45em; margin: 0 auto; }
a { text-decoration: none; color: #CC4B00; }   h1 a { color: #FF5E00; }
@media screen and (max-width: 865px) { #wrap { width: 100%; } }
```

### Chris Olah — https://colah.github.io/
Self-hosts Computer Modern: `fonts/Serif/cmun-serif.css` declares `@font-face { font-family:'CMS'; src:url('cmunrm.woff') }` for roman/bold/italic/bold-italic (cmunrm, cmunbx, cmunti, cmunbi), plus Droid Serif / Droid Sans from Google. Homepage is a thumbnail-per-post list grouped under editorial headings the author invented — "Recent Exciting Things", "Rough Notes" (explicitly labelled lower-quality), "Personal Writing", "Selected Twitter Threads", "Traditional Papers". That candour is itself a design decision. Content caps: `.section-links-ul { max-width: 850px }`, `li { max-width: 800px }`, `p { max-width: 820px }`.

### Arvind Narayanan — https://www.cs.princeton.edu/~arvindn/ (inline CSS, 12.5KB page)
```css
div.innercontainer { width: 980px; }
div.top { display:flex; flex-direction:row; gap:.75rem; max-width:980px; margin:0 auto; margin-top:35px; }
div.topmiddle { text-align: right; width: 30%; }
div.widget.left  { width: 460px; padding-right: 60px; }
div.widget.right { width: 460px; }
p.lead { font-size: 144%; line-height: 150%; }
#navbar { text-align: justify; margin: 0 auto; width: 980px; }
#navbar a { display: inline-block; }
#navbar:after { content: ''; width: 100%; display: inline-block; }  /* forces justification */
```
Google font: `Open Sans:400,600`. The book cover floats left at `height=300` with the intro figure floating right — an editorial spread, not a card grid.

### Michael Bernstein — https://hci.stanford.edu/msb/ (+ /css/msb.css)
```css
body { font-weight: 300; font-size: 16px;
       font-family: 'Helvetica Neue','Source Sans Pro','Open Sans',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif; }
a, a:hover { color: #990615; }                  /* Stanford cardinal */
#msbnav { background-color: #7D0612; }
#msbnav .navbar-brand { font-family:"Oswald",...; font-size:2.5em; font-weight:400;
                        text-transform: uppercase; color:#DCDCDC; }
.sidenav .nav > li > a { display:block; padding: 5px 20px; }
.sidenav .nav > li > a:hover { background-color:#e5e3e9; border-right: 1px solid #990615; }
```
Fonts loaded: `Source Sans Pro:300,400|Oswald:400,700`. Notable content move: student names in each publication's author list carry small inline portrait avatars. Sections: header/mission → bio → publications (2026→2024, thumbnail-left) → teaching by year → contact/office hours → current PhD students / alumni / postdoc alumni with headshots.

### Amy Ko — https://faculty.washington.edu/ajko/ (SvelteKit, component-scoped CSS)
`font-family: Nunito, sans-serif` (+ Noto Emoji), `max-width: 40em` for text, `max-width: 80em` for the shell. 18-item horizontal nav (Latest, Research, Wordplay, Lab, Communities, Publications, Essays, Talks, Classes, Books, Code, Impact, Funding, Travel, Bio, Commitments, Contact, FAQ, CV). The homepage organises research as **"discoveries"** — each is a *claim* with a date range ("Programming languages can be designed to include everyone, 2011-2026"), an image, a row of ~50-60px circular collaborator headshots, and a collapsed `▶ 6 publications` disclosure. Framing research as claims rather than "Research Areas" is the most transferable idea on the page.

### Pascal Michaillat — https://pascalmichaillat.org/ (Hugo + PaperMod)
```css
--main-width: 680px;  --nav-width: 1024px;  --gap: 24px;
--content-size: 1.125rem;  --meta-size: 1.0625rem;  --line-height: 1.5;
--primary: rgb(30,30,30); --secondary: rgb(108,108,108); --tertiary: rgb(165,165,165);
--theme: rgb(255,255,255); --border: rgb(230,230,230); --radius: 8px;
--title-bold: 550; --semibold: 500; --title-height: 1.3;
font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, "segoe ui", Roboto, …, sans-serif;
.main { max-width: calc(var(--main-width) + var(--gap)*2); margin: auto; }
```
Profile image `height=130 width=130`, centered, then h1, then a 3-sentence positioning paragraph, then a row of inline-SVG icons (CV, email, location, office hours, Scholar, YouTube, GitHub), then five pill "buttons" (Book, Dashboard, Papers, Courses, Design). Homepage = 9.2KB. He publishes his templates at /design/ (LaTeX book/paper/beamer/CV, Hugo site, MATLAB figures) under a stated philosophy of "typographical best practices" and "minimalist design". **Caveat:** this is the PaperMod profile mode and it *is* a recognisable template — good numbers, unremarkable identity. Steal the tokens, not the layout.

### Tim Roughgarden — https://timroughgarden.org/
Entire page, 2,568 bytes:
```html
<style> body { font-family: Helvetica, Geneva, Arial, SunSans-Regular, sans-serif } p { font-size:18px } </style>
<table cellpadding=10>
 <td><img src="cce25_1.JPG" width=620 height=420><br><small>Photo credit: Diane Bondareff</small></td>
 <td><h2>Tim Roughgarden</h2> …affiliations, research interests, contact… </td>
</table>
<hr><ul> …11 destination links… </ul><hr>
```
Landscape photo + name block + flat link list. The photo credit is the humanising detail.

### UW Interactive Data Lab — https://idl.uw.edu/ (SvelteKit + Tailwind)
Self-hosted **Avenir** woff2 (`@font-face { font-family: Avenir }` ×6 weights) with fallback `Avenir, "Helvetica Neue", Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif`; mono is the system UI stack. Content `max-width: 56rem` (896px). Nav: home / about / people / papers / blog / code / video + Bluesky. Papers grouped under venue-and-city headers ("VIS 2025 - Vienna, Austria"); each row is thumbnail + title + linked author names + venue/year + PDF/Software/Examples links, with thumbnails **alternating left/right** down the list. A "Spotlight" feature project sits above the papers. Best available model for the RAFT page.

### Others verified
- **Maneesh Agrawala** (graphics.stanford.edu/~maneesh/, 576KB) — Bootstrap + `Cabin:400,500,600,700` + italics. Square-cropped headshot `agrawala-macarthur3-head-square.jpg`. Sections separated by typographic asterisk rules. Reverse-chron pubs with thumbnails and PDF/arXiv/code/video link rows.
- **Cynthia Rudin** (users.cs.duke.edu/~cynthia/) — jemdoc, 13.8KB. `body { font-family: Times, serif }`, blue `#527bbd` / `#022b6d` accents, a left `.menu-category`/`.menu-item` rail, a table-based layout with `<table summary="Table for page layout." id="tlayout">`. Dated but unmistakably personal.
- **Nadia Polikarpova** (cseweb.ucsd.edu/~npolikarpova/styles/ucsd.css) — `.page { width: 800px; margin: 0 auto }`, `body { background-color:#ebecee; color:#3a3a3b; font-size:11pt }` with a white `.page_content` panel, fixed 70px top wrapper holding an 800px purple `#5d4e79` bar, nav in `Lato` 300 at 18pt, links `#50416d`.
- **Jon Kleinberg** (cs.cornell.edu/home/kleinber/) — `<body bgcolor=white text=black link=blue vlink=blue alink=blue>`. Zero CSS. Authority through total austerity.
- **Hal Abelson** (groups.csail.mit.edu/mac/users/hal/) — `<body bgcolor="white" leftmargin="50" rightmargin="50"><font face="arial,geneva,helvetica">`, 200px portrait with `<h6>Portrait by Joi Ito</h6>` credit.
