## B. The templates — so you can recognise the fingerprint

**al-folio** (https://alshedivat.github.io/al-folio/) — the most-forked academic Jekyll theme. Loads, in order: Tailwind, Font Awesome 7.2.0, academicons 1.9.5, scholar-icons 1.0.3, `fonts.googleapis.com/css?family=Roboto:300,400,500,700|Roboto+Slab:100,300,400,500,700|Material+Icons`, and two swappable Pygments highlight themes for light/dark. Card grids, round social icons, dark-mode toggle top-right.

**academicpages / Minimal Mistakes** (https://academicpages.github.io/) — class names give it away: `author__avatar`, `author__bio`, `author__name`, `author__urls social-icons`, `author__desktop`, `greedy-nav`, `btn btn--inverse`, plus Font Awesome + academicons. The sticky left author sidebar with a vertical stack of icon links is *the* academicpages silhouette.

**Heavy CMS tells:** `wp-content/themes/Avada` (Rus), `wp-content/themes/hueman` (Roxy Koll's climate lab), `wp-content/themes/aaron` (Patrick Reed's group), `revslider`, Wix's `wf_<hash>` font names, Google Sites' `gstatic.com/_/atari/`.

